---
description: ASDD contribution rules for this repository
alwaysApply: true
---

This repository is governed by ASDD (Agentic Spec-Driven Development). Read AGENTS.md, the contribution
constitution, before writing code here. These points are a pointer to it, not a second set of rules.

- Disclose the agent in the pull request and the commit trailer, and sign every commit off (`git commit -s`).
- Exactly one lane label per pull request; the set is in `.asdd.yml`.
- A feature or fix points to a spec that defines "done"; only the `chore` lane is spec-exempt.
- You are the developer. The test agents run on a different model, so your own tests are not the deciding check.
- A human merges. Agents review and recommend; you do not merge your own work.

Full guide: docs/guides/bring-your-own-developer.md
